# Styles: a rule inside another applies only inside the elements the outer rule reaches.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Styles · Rules inside rules
	Page:
		Paper: A4
		Margin: 20mm
	Styles:
		For style: card
			Box:
				Margin: 0 0 14 0
				Padding: 12
				Background: sand
				Corner radius: 6
			For element: Paragraph
				Box:
					Margin: 0
				Typography:
					Font: IBM Plex Serif
			For style: body
				Box:
					Margin: 6 0 0 0
					Padding: 8
					Border: 0 0 0 2
					Border color: accent
	Section:
		Text: Styles
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Rules inside rules
		Paragraph: A `For element` or `For style` written inside another rule applies only inside the elements that the outer rule reaches. Here the rules inside `For style: card` change the paragraphs and give the `body` block its look, but only in a card. A style that only has a rule inside another, like `body`, is an error outside it.
			Style: intro
		Text: Outside a card: the usual paragraph
			Style: label
		Paragraph: This paragraph keeps the font and the margin of the base styles.
		Text: Style: card, with its nested For element: Paragraph and For style: body
			Style: label
		Block:
			Style: card
			Paragraph: Inside the card, the paragraphs are serif and have no margin.
			Block:
				Style: body
				Paragraph: This block has the look of body because it is inside a card.
			Stack:
				Item:
					Paragraph: The rule reaches any depth: this paragraph is inside a Stack inside the card.
